                "entry_id": "2b38aca5-65dd-3f95-af32-e1e7e16ae170",
                "word": "reedwork",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29df16d5-b3ce-3c8e-8cdf-3e534a984b5f",
                        "entry_id": "2b38aca5-65dd-3f95-af32-e1e7e16ae170",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Collectively, the reed stops of an organ."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2e1a661-e406-4097-98ae-0d2e2d337701",
                                "sense_id": "29df16d5-b3ce-3c8e-8cdf-3e534a984b5f",
                                "text": "This organ has been praised by many intelligent people, particularly for its reedwork, and I must confess that it gave great pleasure when I examined it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a26359d-2231-4b28-9a36-27fa7a06f51e",
                                "sense_id": "29df16d5-b3ce-3c8e-8cdf-3e534a984b5f",
                                "text": "The finest reedwork was voiced by a Mr. Jeffrey who brought the art of low pressure reed voicing to a very high standard."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2d62536-3221-325c-8c94-2581b5223d0d",
                        "entry_id": "2b38aca5-65dd-3f95-af32-e1e7e16ae170",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The craft of weaving reeds or grasses, or the goods produced by this craft."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b567244b-8ff9-4240-b46b-ff9e8c7731c2",
                                "sense_id": "b2d62536-3221-325c-8c94-2581b5223d0d",
                                "text": "Metal work, leather work, etc., substituted for woodwork and reedwork during other seasons of the year."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cac12e2-2540-42df-8249-897d56d59451",
                                "sense_id": "b2d62536-3221-325c-8c94-2581b5223d0d",
                                "text": "As a hobby, reedwork may well be the most familiar type of basketmaking, but it is not an American Indian tradition."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e7e48e3-42f0-4b90-b0d6-1d9a1130064d",
                                "sense_id": "b2d62536-3221-325c-8c94-2581b5223d0d",
                                "text": "A highly skilled and attractive craft, reedwork can again be seen at Kasubi ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbc6cde2-01f1-4a5b-a817-f49ef1bff44a",
                                "sense_id": "b2d62536-3221-325c-8c94-2581b5223d0d",
                                "text": "there was evidence of excessive cutting of the reedwork, with the tongues loaded to improve regulation, not a Schulze practice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "691c93fa-df1f-489e-9c81-7d1f0f7f5fb3",
                                "sense_id": "b2d62536-3221-325c-8c94-2581b5223d0d",
                                "text": "Others made \"plasticine work, women's wool hats, christmas tree decorations, carding buttons, artificial flowers, reedwork ...brushes ... slippers ...... canvas shoes, dresses, millinery ... shirts ... [ and ] flower buttonholes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
